decisions:
  - id: D-graduation-tiers
    decision: Three-tier automation system with data-driven graduation
    rationale: MCP tools cost ~100-11K tokens per call. Habits cost ~200 tokens. Hooks cost zero. Moving behaviors down the tier stack as compliance data proves consistency saves massive token overhead.
  - id: D-never-graduate
    decision: tool-called and context-checked check types can never graduate to hooks
    rationale: These require the agent to call an MCP tool and reason about the OUTPUT. A hook can verify filesystem state but cannot force cognition.
  - id: D-retroactive-graduation
    decision: 5 seed habits retroactively marked as graduated since stop hook already enforces them
    rationale: purpose-coverage, gates-for-routes, record-lore-for-significant, verify-before-done, and postflight-compliance were duplicated between MCP habits evaluation and the 11-check stop hook. Marking them graduated eliminates the duplication.
  - id: D-hook-source-of-truth
    decision: Hook .sh files in src/commands/hooks/scripts/ are the source of truth, not plugins/
    rationale: The build runs generate-hooks.mjs which copies .sh source files to plugins/ and embeds them in generated-hooks.ts. Editing plugins/ directly gets overwritten on every build.
  - id: D-auto-demotion
    decision: Auto-demote graduated habits after 3 failures in 7 days with 14-day cooldown
    rationale: Graduation must be reversible for safety. If a hook starts failing, the behavior needs to return to agent-visible habit evaluation so the agent can fix the root cause.
  - id: D-view-decomposition
    decision: Decompose BindingsManagerView into 6 sub-views and MainOverlayView into 12 named sections
    rationale: BindingsManagerView at 302 lines was the largest monolith in Conductor. MainOverlayView's mainContent was 100+ lines of inline views. Both needed structural cleanup for maintainability.
errors_encountered:
  - description: Hook scripts in plugins/ kept reverting after every edit
    resolution: 'Discovered generate-hooks.mjs pipeline: source is src/commands/hooks/scripts/*.sh, not plugins/. Edit source, run generator, then build.'
    time_to_fix: 3 attempts before discovering the pipeline
  - description: Context budget heuristic using ${PENDING_COUNT} in template literal was interpreted as JS expression
    resolution: Used $PENDING_COUNT without braces — shell doesn't need them when no ambiguity exists
    time_to_fix: 2 attempts
learnings:
  - Hook shell scripts in plugins/ are auto-generated from src/commands/hooks/scripts/*.sh via generate-hooks.mjs — always edit source .sh files then run the generator
  - Template literals in generated-hooks.ts interpret ${} as JS expressions — use $VAR not ${VAR} for shell variables in embedded hooks
  - The stop hook already checks 11 compliance items that overlap with 5 of 13 seed habits — graduating these eliminates ~750 tokens/session of duplicate evaluation
  - SentinelEvent needed Hashable conformance for SwiftUI .popover(item:) — added == and hash(into:) based on id field
  - Context budget can be estimated heuristically by edit count in the post-write hook — 30+ edits correlates with high context usage, zero token cost vs ~600 tokens for manual paradigm_context_check polling
